# Blocker E-9 — the voice/face entity whitelist is qingshan-only
#
# PROBLEM
#   tools/multimodal_character_binding_guard.py held ENTITY_ALIASES as a closed
#   24-entry dict, every entry belonging to the qingshan line (陈迹/白鲤/…).
#   The nalu line's six ids (qinming, luze, liangwanqing, zhouapo,
#   yangyongqing, villager_a) are absent, so every nalu video task would report
#   UNREGISTERED_ENTITY_BINDING (:325-330). Its three tenant authority files
#   (voice registry, agentcut voice policy, character asset registry) were also
#   hardcoded to configs/ paths that do not exist in this portable clone, so
#   the guard raised FileNotFoundError before it could report anything.
#   tools/agentcut_character_voice_reference_guard.py additionally asserts that
#   its two EXEMPT ids (chenji, baili) are LOCKED in the registry, which fails
#   on any registry that legitimately contains neither.
#
# CHOSEN FIX — env-var extension point, not hardcoding
#   1. QINGSHAN_ENTITY_REGISTRY -> a JSON that ADDS entities. The loader is
#      fail-closed and additive only: it rejects a wrong schema, a non-object
#      entity_aliases, a non-identifier entity id, any attempt to redefine a
#      built-in entity, a missing display name or registry id, and any display
#      name already bound to another entity. It therefore cannot relax, remove
#      or shadow an existing binding.
#   2. QINGSHAN_VOICE_REGISTRY / QINGSHAN_AGENTCUT_VOICE_POLICY /
#      QINGSHAN_CHARACTER_REGISTRY relocate the three tenant authority files.
#      Location only: the files are still loaded eagerly and still have to
#      exist and parse, so a wrong override fails exactly as a missing default
#      did. QINGSHAN_VOICE_REGISTRY is the name tools/speaker_voice_contract.py:78
#      already used, so this makes the guards agree with the contract compiler
#      instead of contradicting it.
#   3. EXEMPT is now INTERSECTED with the registry's own
#      policy.only_legacy_native_voice_exemptions — a key
#      tools/generate_agentcut_character_voice_references.py:412 already
#      writes. The set can only ever SHRINK; declaring an entity that is not
#      already exempt raises. Omitting the key preserves the previous
#      behaviour byte for byte.
#
# WHY NO CHECK IS WEAKENED
#   * No threshold, status set, required field or failure code was changed.
#   * Nothing was added to EXEMPT and nothing can be: escalation raises.
#     The nalu registry declares [] , i.e. STRICTER than the default.
#   * ENTITY_ALIASES only grows, and only with entities that carry both a
#     display name and a registry id — which is exactly what makes
#     MISSING_ENTITY_BINDING / CANONICAL_VISUAL_REFERENCE_MISMATCH apply to
#     them. Registering nalu's characters SUBJECTS them to the guard; it does
#     not exempt them.
#   * With no env var set, both modules behave identically to before.
#
# VERIFICATION
#   tools/tests/test_multimodal_character_binding_guard.py            17 passed
#   tools/tests/test_agentcut_character_voice_reference_guard.py       2 pre-existing
#     failures (KeyError 'identity' in performance_brief_sha256), IDENTICAL
#     before and after this patch — confirmed by rerunning the suite against
#     the pristine file.
#   python -m qingshan_engine.cli test -> 376 tests, OK (skipped=11),
#     {"schema":"qingshan.portable_ci.v2","status":"PASS","failures":[]}
#
# COMPANION RUNTIME FILES (not part of this diff, live in nalu_runtime)
#   $RUNTIME_ROOT/runtime/nalu_entity_registry.json
#   $RUNTIME_ROOT/runtime/voice_registry.json
#   $RUNTIME_ROOT/runtime/agentcut_character_voice_reference_policy_nalu_v1.json
